{
  "table_id": "Table_S19",
  "display_number": "S19",
  "title": "Supplementary Table S19. CHARLS-adapted PhenoAge biomarker set.",
  "panel": "",
  "panel_title": "",
  "notes_before": [
    "The original NHANES PhenoAge framework uses chronological age and nine blood biomarkers. This table records the documented CHARLS mapping: six clinical measures in the original framework and five additional measures, with albumin, alkaline phosphatase and red cell distribution width unavailable. The additional measures capture different physiological information and are not equivalent substitutes. Implementation of this mapping in the stored primary score could not be verified from the available code. hs-CRP, high-sensitivity C-reactive protein; MCV, mean corpuscular volume; HbA1c, glycated haemoglobin; BUN, blood urea nitrogen; ALP, alkaline phosphatase; RDW, red cell distribution width."
  ],
  "notes_after": [
    "The documentation describes mortality-based calibration using follow-up through 2020, followed by standardisation and rescaling of a linear predictor. The original calibration code linked to the stored primary BAA was unavailable. The separate recalibration in Table S25 uses a different documented predictor specification and does not verify this mapping. Source: CHARLS venous blood; the documented fasting restriction was at least 8 hours."
  ],
